This crate is an original implementation for nv-rs of the role the script extender plugin of
Tale of Two Wastelands plays for TTW's own scripts (the plugin answers to `ttw_nvse`; TTW's
readers call it ROOGNVSE). It contains no code of the plugin and no decompiled code, and none
was read for it: it is written from public behaviour only.

Sources used (2026-11-20):
- the command names, opcodes and parameter counts: a third-party dump of the plugin's command
  list (nvse-lsp, resources/functions/ttw_nvse.json): TTW_ShowGeneProjector 0x3800,
  TTW_GetPlugins 0x3806 (returns an array), TTW_EnableRadioFix 0x3808 (one integer). The three
  opcodes were checked against the compiled scripts of the installed TaleOfTwoWastelands.esm
  (the opcode u16 in each SCDA whose SCTX calls the command); they match;
- how each command is called and what the caller does with the answer: the script text (SCTX)
  of TTW's own scripts in TaleOfTwoWastelands.esm (its start-up quest script reads
  `aLoadedMods[iModIndex][1]` of TTW_GetPlugins and flags `< 1.3` as a mod not converted for
  TTW; TTW_EnableRadioFix is called with 0 or 1);
- the engine's own data: the data handler's list of loaded files and each file's header version
  (the HEDR version float), and xNVSE's arrays.

What each command is built from:
- TTW_GetPlugins: the TTW script's use (an array of [name, version] pairs, element 1 a number
  compared with 1.3) and the engine's loaded-file list. Built.
- TTW_EnableRadioFix: the TTW script's calls (one integer, 0 or 1). It STORES the value in the
  plugin's state. The radio fix itself is NOT built: nothing in the engine changes behaviour
  because of the value.
- TTW_ShowGeneProjector: opens the gene projector character menu. NOT built: its record name is
  registered so the script error log names it, with no handler; a script that calls it stops
  for that run.

Unverified: the DLL file name (ttw_nvse.dll is the plugin's name plus the extension, not read
from a public document) and the version the plugin hands xNVSE (1 is a guess). The name
"ttw_nvse" is exact (TTW asks IsPluginInstalled ttw_nvse). The parameter name and help text of
each command are not known; none is claimed.
